    "narrative": "For today's slate, our lineup leans heavily into aggressive base-running and high-floor production against soft-tossing rotations. **James Wood** (78.42) anchors the offense, benefiting from an elite park factor (+16%) and a favorable matchup against Trevor Rogers. He is joined in the top tier by **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) and **Corbin Carroll** (75.42). **Mickey Moniak** is particularly intriguing; while Taj Bradley presents a moderate strikeout threat, his tendency to allow stolen bases (100% SB rating in our model) combined with **Mickey Moniak**\u2019s +14% platoon edge makes him a primary engine for our SB-starved Roto campaign. **Tyler Soderstrom** (71.48) also deserves a spotlight, as his +6% dynamic platoon advantage against Walbert Ure\u00f1a creates a prime environment for an extra-base hit.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was excluding **Travis Bazzana** (51.16). While he boasts a strong projected +10% order bonus from his assumed lead-off spot, he ultimately fell short because he lacks the high-leverage stolen base indicators provided by the current starters. We also need to keep a close watch on **Jose Caballero** (61.88); while his profile is excellent due to his +13% platoon edge against Payton Tolle, there is a 35% rain risk looming over his contest. Should that game get delayed or postponed, we will be forced to pivot, likely looking for a safer floor from the utility bench. Finally, monitor the official lineups, as our reliance on **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, and **Brice Turang** currently rests on favorable, yet unconfirmed, batting order projections. Should **Brice Turang** drop out of the #3 spot, his efficiency score\u2014currently bolstered by a +6% order bonus\u2014will require an immediate re-evaluation.",
